#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:16
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:18
msgid ""
"This plugin requires minimum **Node.js 6.11.5**, **webpack 4**, "
"**TypeScript 2.1** and optionally **ESLint 6** (which itself requires "
"minimum **Node.js 8.10.0**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:20
msgid ""
"If you depend on **webpack 2**, **webpack 3**, or **tslint 4**, please "
"use [older version](https://github.com/TypeStrong/fork-ts-checker-"
"webpack-plugin/tree/v3.1.1) of the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:30
msgid ""
"Basic webpack config (with [ts-loader](https://github.com/TypeStrong/ts-"
"loader))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:54
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:56
msgid ""
"There was already similar solution - [awesome-typescript-"
"loader](https://github.com/s-panferov/awesome-typescript-loader). You can"
" add `CheckerPlugin` and delegate checker to the separate process. The "
"problem with `awesome-typescript-loader` was that, in our case, it was a "
"lot slower than [ts-loader](https://github.com/TypeStrong/ts-loader) on "
"an incremental build (~20s vs ~3s). Secondly, we used "
"[tslint](https://palantir.github.io/tslint) and we wanted to run this, "
"along with type checker, in a separate process. This is why this plugin "
"was created. To provide better performance, the plugin reuses Abstract "
"Syntax Trees between compilations and shares these trees with TSLint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:63
msgid "Modules resolution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:65
msgid ""
"It's very important to be aware that **this plugin uses "
"[TypeScript](https://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript)'s, not "
"[webpack](https://github.com/webpack/webpack)'s modules resolution**. It "
"means that you have to setup `tsconfig.json` correctly. For example if "
"you set `files: ['./src/someFile.ts']` in `tsconfig.json`, this plugin "
"will check only `someFile.ts` for semantic errors. It's because of "
"performance. The goal of this plugin is to be _as fast as possible_. With"
" TypeScript's module resolution we don't have to wait for webpack to "
"compile files (which traverses dependency graph during compilation) - we "
"have a full list of files from the begin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:71
msgid ""
"To debug TypeScript's modules resolution, you can use `tsc "
"--traceResolution` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:73
msgid "ESLint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:75
msgid ""
"[ESLint is the future of linting in the TypeScript "
"world.](https://eslint.org/blog/2019/01/future-typescript-eslint) If "
"you'd like to use eslint with the plugin, supply this option: `eslint: "
"true` and ensure you have the relevant dependencies installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:77
msgid ""
"`yarn add eslint @typescript-eslint/parser @typescript-eslint/eslint-"
"plugin --dev`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:79
msgid ""
"You should have an ESLint configuration file in your root project "
"directory. Here is a sample `.eslintrc.js` configuration for a TypeScript"
" project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:101
msgid ""
"There's a good explanation on setting up TypeScript ESLint support by "
"Robert Cooper [here](https://dev.to/robertcoopercode/using-eslint-and-"
"prettier-in-a-typescript-project-53jb)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:103
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:105
msgid ""
"**tsconfig** `string`: Path to _tsconfig.json_ file. Default: "
"`path.resolve(compiler.options.context, './tsconfig.json')`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:108
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**compilerOptions** `object`: Allows overriding TypeScript options. "
"Should be specified in the same format as you would do for the "
"`compilerOptions` property in tsconfig.json. Default: `{}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:111
msgid "**eslint** `true | undefined`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:113
msgid "If `true`, this activates eslint support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:115
msgid "**eslintOptions** `object`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:117
msgid ""
"Options that can be used to initialise ESLint. See "
"https://eslint.org/docs/developer-guide/nodejs-api#cliengine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:119
msgid ""
"**async** `boolean`: True by default - `async: false` can block webpack's"
" emit to wait for type checker/linter and to add errors to the webpack's "
"compilation. We recommend to set this to `false` in projects where type "
"checking is faster than webpack's build - it's better for integration "
"with other plugins. Another scenario where you might want to set this to "
"`false` is if you use the `overlay` functionality of `webpack-dev-"
"server`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:123
msgid ""
"**ignoreDiagnostics** `number[]`: List of TypeScript diagnostic codes to "
"ignore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:126
msgid "**ignoreLints** `string[]`: List of eslint rule names to ignore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:129
msgid "**ignoreLintWarnings** `boolean`: If true, will ignore all lint warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:132
msgid ""
"**reportFiles** `string[]`: Only report errors on files matching these "
"glob patterns. This can be useful when certain types definitions have "
"errors that are not fatal to your application. Default: `[]`. Please note"
" that this may behave unexpectedly if using the incremental API as the "
"incremental API doesn't look for global and semantic errors [if it has "
"already found syntactic "
"errors](https://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript/blob/89386ddda7dafc63cb35560e05412487f47cc267/src/compiler/watch.ts#L141)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:142
msgid ""
"**logger** `object`: Logger instance. It should be object that implements"
" method: `error`, `warn`, `info`. Default: `console`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:145
msgid ""
"**formatter** `'default' | 'codeframe' | (issue: Issue) => string)`: "
"Formatter for issues and lints. By default uses `default` formatter. You "
"can also pass your own formatter as a function (see `src/issue/` and "
"`src/formatter/` for API reference)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:149
msgid ""
"**formatterOptions** `object`: Options passed to formatters (currently "
"only `codeframe` - see [available "
"options](https://babeljs.io/docs/en/next/babel-code-frame.html#options))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:152
msgid ""
"**silent** `boolean`: If `true`, logger will not be used. Default: "
"`false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:155
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**checkSyntacticErrors** `boolean`: This option is useful if you're using"
" ts-loader in `happyPackMode` with "
"[HappyPack](https://github.com/amireh/happypack) or [thread-"
"loader](https://github.com/webpack-contrib/thread-loader) to parallelise "
"your builds. If `true` it will ensure that the plugin checks for _both_ "
"syntactic errors (eg `const array = [{} {}];`) and semantic errors (eg "
"`const x: number = '1';`). By default the plugin only checks for semantic"
" errors. This is because when ts-loader is used in `transpileOnly` mode, "
"ts-loader will still report syntactic errors. When used in "
"`happyPackMode` it does not. Default: `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:158
msgid ""
"**memoryLimit** `number`: Memory limit for service process in MB. If "
"service exits with allocation failed error, increase this number. "
"Default: `2048`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:161
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**vue** `boolean | { enabled: boolean, compiler: string }`: If `true` or "
"`enabled: true`, the linter and compiler will process VueJs single-file-"
"component (.vue) files. See the [Vue "
"section](https://github.com/TypeStrong/fork-ts-checker-webpack-"
"plugin#vue) further down for information on how to correctly setup your "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:165
msgid ""
"**useTypescriptIncrementalApi** `boolean`: If true, the plugin will use "
"incremental compilation API introduced in TypeScript 2.7. Defaults to "
"`true` when working with TypeScript 3+ and `false` when below 3. The "
"default can be overridden by directly specifying a value. Don't use it "
"together with VueJs enabled - it's not supported yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:169
msgid ""
"**measureCompilationTime** `boolean`: If true, the plugin will measure "
"the time spent inside the compilation code. This may be useful to compare"
" modes, especially if there are other loaders/plugins involved in the "
"compilation. **requires Node.js >= 8.5.0**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:173
msgid ""
"**typescript** `string`: If supplied this is a custom path where "
"`typescript` can be found. Defaults to `require.resolve('typescript')`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:176
msgid ""
"**resolveModuleNameModule** and **resolveTypeReferenceDirectiveModule** "
"`string`: Both of those options refer to files on the disk that "
"respectively export a `resolveModuleName` or a "
"`resolveTypeReferenceDirectiveModule` function. These functions will be "
"used to resolve the import statements and the `<reference types=\"...\">`"
" directives instead of the default TypeScript implementation. Check the "
"following code for an example of what those functions should look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:220
msgid "Different behaviour in watch mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:222
msgid ""
"If you turn on [webpacks watch "
"mode](https://webpack.js.org/configuration/watch/#watch) the `fork-ts-"
"checker-notifier-webpack-plugin` will take care of logging type errors, "
"_not_ webpack itself. That means if you set `silent: true` you won't see "
"type errors in your console in watch mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:224
msgid ""
"You can either set `silent: false` to show the logging from `fork-ts-"
"checker-notifier-webpack-plugin` _or_ set `async: false`. Now webpack "
"itself will log type errors again, but note that this can slow down your "
"builds depending on the size of your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:226
msgid "Notifier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:228
msgid ""
"You may already be using the excellent [webpack-"
"notifier](https://github.com/Turbo87/webpack-notifier) plugin to make "
"build failures more obvious in the form of system notifications. There's "
"an equivalent notifier plugin designed to work with the `fork-ts-checker-"
"webpack-plugin`. It is the `fork-ts-checker-notifier-webpack-plugin` and "
"can be found [here](https://github.com/johnnyreilly/fork-ts-checker-"
"notifier-webpack-plugin). This notifier deliberately has a similar API as"
" the `webpack-notifier` plugin to make migration easier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:230
msgid "Known Issue Watching Non-Emitting Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:232
msgid ""
"At present there is an issue with the plugin regarding the triggering of "
"type-checking when a change is made in a source file that will not emit "
"js. If you have a file which contains only `interface`s and / or `type`s "
"then changes to it will **not** trigger the type checker whilst in watch "
"mode. Sorry about that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin_README.md:234
msgid ""
"We hope this will be resolved in future; the issue can be tracked "
"[here](https://github.com/TypeStrong/fork-ts-checker-webpack-"
"plugin/issues/36)."
msgstr ""

